-- allium: 3

-- Module: config.
-- Scope: every label and annotation knarr reads on a Deployment, its type,
-- default, validation and the behaviour on an invalid value; refusal of
-- unsupported workload kinds (§3 non-goals); and the target set that discovery
-- derives from it inside knarr's one namespace (§4, §9.1, §9.18).
-- Owner: ticket 19. Override defaults come from 18, 20, 21, 23 and 24. The
-- decided discovery LIST and one install per namespace are built by the round-2
-- spec-then-build ticket 31.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "§9.1 Schema: the label and annotation key prefix knarr owns, and which keys are labels and which are annotations."
open question "§9.1 Opt-in: how a Deployment opts in, and what the discovery LIST selects on (§4)."
open question "§9.1 Overrides: which tuning values a Deployment may override (endpoint, the thresholds and margin, unreachable windows, staleness, poll and write limits) and the valid range of each, taken from the owning ticket."
open question "§9.1 Opt-in for safe-to-evict: how a workload enables the per-workload safe-to-evict policy, which is off by default (§6)."
open question "§9.1 Invalid values: what knarr does with an unparsable or out-of-range value (ignore the key, ignore the workload, Event)."
open question "§9.1 Unsupported kinds: whether knarr refuses or warns when pointed at a StatefulSet, Job or DaemonSet, and how (§3 non-goals)."
